=== Notes (honesty covenant) ===
- Capability AVAILABLE (not BLOCKED): Kotlin 2.4.0 (>= the prompt's >=2.2.x), AGP 8.9.2, Compose BOM 2026.04.01,
  Material 3, minSdk 26 (API 26+/Android 8). Build/test/lint all run on this runner (JDK 21 JBR + Android SDK).
- Surface shape: AddAnnotationPopover is a CONTROLLED-INPUT modal. The web source's only hook is useTranslation;
  it performs no data fetch, owns no store, and makes no HTTP call - the assembled annotation is handed to the
  parent via the onAdd callback (native: onAdd(AnnotationResult)), exactly like the web onAdd prop. There is no
  S8 data store to bind, so the prompt's generic loading/empty/error/stale/offline DATA states do not exist in the
  source and are not fabricated. The states that DO exist are all reproduced, no hidden surfaces:
    * fixed-date branch  -> the raw timestamp shown as muted text (web editableDate=false).
    * editable-date branch -> a capped Material 3 DatePicker (selectable <= today; web max=today) seeded from the
      timestamp via toDateInputValue (web useEffect re-sync).
    * label-required submit gate -> the Add action is disabled until a non-blank label is typed (web
      disabled={!label.trim()}); buildResult returns null (no-op) for a blank label or unresolved occurred-at.
    * category selection -> six colour-coded pills (FilterChip, TalkBack-announced selected/unselected), accents
      mirror the web ANNOTATION_COLORS constant.
    * dismiss/submit -> onCancel / onAdd.
- i18n (P1/S10): every Kotlin string resolves via stringResource from the EXISTING generated catalog
  (translation_annotation_* + translation_common_*); no new keys, no English literals in .kt. The two web keys
  annotation.labelPlaceholder / annotation.descPlaceholder are referenced verbatim; those two lines carry a
  "// parity:allow web i18n key name" opt-out for the placeholder gate (PLACEHOLDER_ALLOWED=2, COUNT=0).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): one-shot PII-safe view.opened emitted with surface slug "AddAnnotationPopover" (carries no
  label/description/timestamp).
- Tests: AddAnnotationPopoverModelTest (off-device adapter/per-branch/diagnostics coverage, executed by the
  testReleaseUnitTest step above) + AddAnnotationPopoverUiTest (instrumented a11y/UI: label presence, fixed vs
  editable date branches, label-required gate, category-select hand-off, cancel). The UI test compiles in the
  androidTest source set and runs under connectedAndroidTest on a device/emulator - not part of this offline gate.
- androidTest note: the androidTest source set has PRE-EXISTING, unrelated compile errors in sibling files
  (assertExists/assertDoesNotExist in FSMStateDiagram + several dashboard-widget tests) that are OUTSIDE this
  surface's allowed files and OUTSIDE this gate. This surface's own UI test passed :android:ktlintAndroidTestSourceSetCheck.
- Files beyond the templated allow-list: the two test files (acceptance requires adapter + per-state UI + a11y
  tests). No res/values string bundle was needed - every i18n key already exists in the generated P1/S10 catalog.
